Package: ukbioprepr
Type: Package
Title: Preparing Environmental Data for Biodiveristy Modelling in the UK
Version: 0.1.0
Author: C. R. Rush
Maintainer: C. R. Rush <cr23569@essex.ac.uk>
Description: ukbioprepr provides functions for downloading raster files and extracting data on climate, soil and land cover variables for the United Kingdom. 
  Extraction functions can handle grid references in both Irish Grid for Northern Ireland, and British National Grid for the whole of the UK as well as co-ordinates in different co-ordinate reference systems. 
  Downloadable data products created through leveraging existing open-source data sets fill any gaps to produce environmental measurements for biodiversity time-series data since 2000. 
  ukbioprepr has been developed to address issues associated with environmental data preparation for UK biodiversity datasets, as well as expedite and streamline this important process. It provides a user-friendly toolkit for environmental data wrangling.
  The functions included in this package facilitate UK biodiversity modelling which is valuable for those working towards important biodiversity targets. 
